.TH heliosctl-streams-start 1 0.3.0 "heliosctl 0.3.0" "Helios Manual"
.SH NAME
heliosctl\-streams\-start \- Start a stream (desired state live)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBheliosctl streams start\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-endpoint\fR] [\fB\-\-wait\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-client\-token\fR] [\fB\-\-region\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIDEVICE\fR> <\fISTREAM\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Start a stream (desired state live)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Check the input and print the request without sending it
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON document on stdout, and errors as JSON on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fI<ENDPOINT>\fR
The Control API\*(Aqs base URL (…/dev)
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR
Wait until the device has applied the change
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR
The AWS profile: one that assumes helios\-operator [default: helios\-operator]
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<TIMEOUT>\fR [default: 60]
How long \-\-wait waits, in seconds
.TP
\fB\-\-client\-token\fR \fI<CLIENT_TOKEN>\fR
Makes the change safe to retry (default: a new random one)
.TP
\fB\-\-region\fR \fI<REGION>\fR
The AWS region [default: the profile\*(Aqs]
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIDEVICE\fR>
A device ID (d\-…) or thing name (t\-…)
.TP
<\fISTREAM\fR>
The stream\*(Aqs name
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBheliosctl\fR(1), for exit status, environment, files and security.
